---
import manifest from "../generated/manifest.json";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageHeader from "../components/PageHeader.astro";
const profile = manifest.documents.filter((document) => document.section === "about");
---
<BaseLayout title="About" description="About Ayush and these notes." generatedAt={manifest.generatedAt}>
  <PageHeader
    eyebrow="About"
    title="About me"
    intro="I’m Ayush Madhukar, a computer engineering student in the Bay Area. Technology is my main hobby, and I spend a lot of time figuring out what hardware and software can do once the defaults get out of the way."
    count={profile.length}
  />
  <div class="prose overview-prose">
    <p>I have always liked finding the capabilities and limits of things. When I was younger that meant jailbreaking devices and running emulators on hardware that was not meant to do it. I still approach technology the same way: set it up, take it apart, compare options, break something, and learn enough to fix it.</p>
    <p>Lately I have been working on local AI, a Proxmox homelab, Linux computers, audio systems, cameras, and the Obsidian vault that feeds these pages.</p>
    <h2>About these notes</h2>
    <p>This is not a copy of my vault. It removes old duplicates and internal maintenance notes, then turns the useful parts into normal pages with links between them. It updates when I change the vault.</p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
